WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.101
Your product ships every week. Your docs fall behind.

00:00:04.451 --> 00:00:08.626
Readers give up halfway down a page. AI agents read it too.

00:00:08.676 --> 00:00:10.590
And you can't see where it goes wrong.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.733
Markdrop Guides. Docs that show you what to fix next.

00:00:15.783 --> 00:00:24.374
Start with the docs you have. Import a GitHub repository: Markdown, GitBook, Mintlify, Docusaurus or MkDocs.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.874
Turn on Keep in sync, and every push updates the guide.

00:00:28.724 --> 00:00:32.238
Once readers arrive, Guides watches what they run into:

00:00:32.288 --> 00:00:40.645
the section where they leave, searches that find nothing, questions Ask AI couldn't answer, the moment a video loses them, broken links.

00:00:40.695 --> 00:00:44.422
It all becomes one list, ranked by how many readers it affects.

00:00:45.072 --> 00:00:50.975
Riya opens the top item. Forty-two percent of readers stop at Install the CLI.

00:00:51.025 --> 00:00:58.977
AI drafts a fix from the evidence. It opens in the editor as a suggestion, and nothing changes until she accepts it.

00:00:59.027 --> 00:01:01.815
She publishes, and the item moves to Fixed.

00:01:02.665 --> 00:01:06.073
Your docs have a second audience now: AI agents.

00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:11.983
Every guide serves llms.txt, Markdown pages and an MCP server.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:18.534
Agent reads are counted apart from people, and the Fix list flags pages agents find hard to use.

00:01:19.384 --> 00:01:21.746
Show the real thing, not a screenshot.

00:01:21.796 --> 00:01:30.942
Embed a live demo, a video or a PDF right in the page. Demos run in a locked sandbox, with a text version for search and AI.

00:01:30.992 --> 00:01:34.784
And when a video loses viewers, that shows up in the Fix list too.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.337
Some pages are only for one customer.

00:01:38.387 --> 00:01:45.314
Make a page or a section private: for your team, for anyone with a Northwind email, or behind a password.

00:01:45.364 --> 00:01:49.518
Dana signs in with a link we email her. Everyone else sees a lock.

00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:51.333
Private pages are free.

00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:57.980
Pick one of fourteen themes, or build your own, and put it on your domain with one DNS record.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:05.234
Readers get search, Ask AI answers that link to the source, an API reference with Try it, and a changelog.

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:11.070
Markdrop Guides. Free while in beta, at markdrop.in/guides.
